1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:05,181
Your Terraform apply just removed a production virtual server.

2
00:00:05,181 --> 00:00:06,722
The plan said minus one.

3
00:00:06,722 --> 00:00:09,676
Nobody read it. The change went through at two

4
00:00:09,676 --> 00:00:12,822
in the morning, and the incident bridge opened at

5
00:00:12,822 --> 00:00:13,079
six.

6
00:00:13,829 --> 00:00:15,878
What if Claude read every plan,

7
00:00:15,878 --> 00:00:18,523
explained every change in plain English,

8
00:00:18,523 --> 00:00:22,291
flagged the common mistakes before they reached a device,

9
00:00:22,291 --> 00:00:25,266
and the apply ran only after a person clicked

10
00:00:25,266 --> 00:00:28,506
approve? That is Terraform and GitHub automation,

11
00:00:28,506 --> 00:00:30,489
done with Claude, done safely.

12
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:36,379
Gennoor Tech presents Terraform and GitHub Automation with Claude.

13
00:00:37,129 --> 00:00:40,193
One repository. One pull request per change.

14
00:00:40,193 --> 00:00:42,491
You learn Terraform step by step,

15
00:00:42,491 --> 00:00:45,556
you learn the mistakes that burn real teams,

16
00:00:45,556 --> 00:00:48,202
and you put Claude to work as planner,

17
00:00:48,202 --> 00:00:52,102
explainer and reviewer. Claude drafts the code and reads

18
00:00:52,102 --> 00:00:55,445
the plan. Deterministic pipelines run the apply.

19
00:00:55,445 --> 00:00:58,787
A human approves anything that touches a device,

20
00:00:58,787 --> 00:01:00,528
and every step is logged.

21
00:01:00,528 --> 00:01:03,453
By the end you own a repository your whole

22
00:01:03,453 --> 00:01:04,637
team can work in.

23
00:01:05,387 --> 00:01:09,109
You start with infrastructure as code for network and

24
00:01:09,109 --> 00:01:12,059
load balancer teams. Providers, resources,

25
00:01:12,059 --> 00:01:15,359
variables, outputs and state, written in H C L.

26
00:01:15,359 --> 00:01:17,325
Then you set up Claude Code,

27
00:01:17,325 --> 00:01:19,502
the Claude Agent S D K and an M

28
00:01:19,502 --> 00:01:22,382
C P server that exposes the Terraform C L

29
00:01:22,382 --> 00:01:25,050
I as tools, so the agent can run init,

30
00:01:25,050 --> 00:01:28,280
validate and plan, but never apply on its own.

31
00:01:28,280 --> 00:01:31,651
You will see exactly which tools the agent holds

32
00:01:31,651 --> 00:01:33,196
and which it does not.

33
00:01:33,946 --> 00:01:35,912
Then Terraform, step by step.

34
00:01:35,912 --> 00:01:39,166
Init, plan, apply, and the state file that makes

35
00:01:39,166 --> 00:01:41,606
it all work. You read a plan line by

36
00:01:41,606 --> 00:01:45,266
line, you import a virtual server that already exists,

37
00:01:45,266 --> 00:01:48,113
and you move to remote state with locking,

38
00:01:48,113 --> 00:01:50,011
workspaces for dev and prod,

39
00:01:50,011 --> 00:01:52,790
and modules you can reuse for every site.

40
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:56,096
Day two opens with the common mistakes.

41
00:01:56,096 --> 00:02:00,027
Unpinned provider versions. Secrets hard coded in variables.

42
00:02:00,027 --> 00:02:01,993
Count where for each belonged.

43
00:02:01,993 --> 00:02:03,959
A state file committed to Git.

44
00:02:03,959 --> 00:02:06,580
A targeted apply that left drift behind.

45
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:08,218
Each mistake gets a name,

46
00:02:08,218 --> 00:02:09,528
a symptom and a fix.

47
00:02:09,528 --> 00:02:11,756
You reproduce each one in the lab,

48
00:02:11,756 --> 00:02:14,246
then wire in the checks that catch it:

49
00:02:14,246 --> 00:02:18,112
terraform format, validate, tflint and a Claude review that

50
00:02:18,112 --> 00:02:20,536
names the mistake and cites the line.

51
00:02:21,286 --> 00:02:25,232
Then GitHub. Branches, commits, a git ignore that keeps

52
00:02:25,232 --> 00:02:28,102
state and secrets out of the repository,

53
00:02:28,102 --> 00:02:30,828
pull requests with required reviewers,

54
00:02:30,828 --> 00:02:33,268
code owners and branch protection.

55
00:02:33,268 --> 00:02:36,855
GitHub Actions runs plan on every pull request and

56
00:02:36,855 --> 00:02:40,299
apply only on merge, with the plan output posted

57
00:02:40,299 --> 00:02:43,168
as a comment for the team to read before

58
00:02:43,168 --> 00:02:46,110
anyone clicks approve. Guardrails follow:

59
00:02:46,110 --> 00:02:48,406
an allow list of resource types,

60
00:02:48,406 --> 00:02:51,491
a block on destroy without a change ticket,

61
00:02:51,491 --> 00:02:54,217
approval gates in GitHub environments,

62
00:02:54,217 --> 00:02:57,445
and an audit record for every plan and apply.

63
00:02:58,195 --> 00:03:01,503
Day three brings the agent into the review loop.

64
00:03:01,503 --> 00:03:04,328
An Agent S D K application reads the plan

65
00:03:04,328 --> 00:03:05,086
as J S O N,

66
00:03:05,086 --> 00:03:08,186
returns a structured verdict with risk level,

67
00:03:08,186 --> 00:03:11,425
affected resources and a plain English summary,

68
00:03:11,425 --> 00:03:13,699
and posts it to the pull request.

69
00:03:13,699 --> 00:03:16,248
It never merges and it never applies.

70
00:03:16,248 --> 00:03:18,660
When it cannot classify a resource,

71
00:03:18,660 --> 00:03:20,864
it says so and asks for a human.

72
00:03:21,614 --> 00:03:26,297
Finally, the devices themselves. The F5 BIG-IP provider for

73
00:03:26,297 --> 00:03:29,471
virtual servers, pools and certificates.

74
00:03:29,471 --> 00:03:32,645
The Citrix A D C provider for NetScaler.

75
00:03:32,645 --> 00:03:35,820
The Cisco A C I provider for tenants and

76
00:03:35,820 --> 00:03:40,423
bridge domains. And Python wrappers for Radware Alteon and

77
00:03:40,423 --> 00:03:44,946
other load balancers (Anaya LB) where no provider exists,

78
00:03:44,946 --> 00:03:48,120
so one workflow covers the whole estate.

79
00:03:48,870 --> 00:03:52,404
Every lab runs against a shared GitHub organization and

80
00:03:52,404 --> 00:03:54,010
lab devices in a sandbox.

81
00:03:54,010 --> 00:03:56,387
Nothing you do in the lab can reach a

82
00:03:56,387 --> 00:03:59,599
production device. You will commit a state file on

83
00:03:59,599 --> 00:04:01,591
purpose, watch Claude catch it,

84
00:04:01,591 --> 00:04:04,160
break a plan with an unintended destroy,

85
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:07,051
and see the approval gate hold until a person

86
00:04:07,051 --> 00:04:07,629
says yes.

